[00:33.07]Conversation One
[00:35.15]M: OK, Mary! Can you tell me about your English success story?
[00:40.25]W: It's not a success story, but I can tell you how I learned. 
[00:45.49]I don't think I learned English as a foreign language, because I loved to listen to music, especially rock and roll, when I was a teenager. 
[00:54.57]When you love music, you want to sing with it, so that you can memorize the whole lyrics and you know the stuff. 
[01:03.11]So to me, it was like a hobby. It was pure fun for me.
[01:07.77]M: Wow, that's great! So did you listen without reading the words and the lyrics, or did you just listen and read the lyrics at the same time?
[01:16.73]W: Hmm, both! 
[01:18.44]Sometimes I'd see some words which I didn't understand, so I'd look them up in the dictionary and check the meanings. 
[01:25.51]Things were always like this.
[01:27.71]M: So did you do anything else besides music?
[01:30.80]W: What else? Yeah, the movie! 
[01:34.16]I loved The Blues Brothers, which was one of my favorite movies, because that movie was interesting. 
[01:41.24]I think it was the funniest movie and the greatest comedy in history. 
[01:46.80]It was famous for its music, and I have the CD in my room.
[01:51.25]M: You have it in your room?
[01:52.91]W: Yeah!
[01:53.54]M: Really?
[01:54.52]W: Yeah, I do. So I saw that movie so many times. 
[01:59.31]I don't remember how many times I saw that. 
[02:02.31]After the repetition...you know, after watching the same movie so many times you can memorize a whole, like words and sentences, what John Belushi was saying, what Dan Aykroyd was saying...
[02:17.32]So it was a great study for me!
[02:19.68]M: Wow! That's great.
[02:21.53]W: But at that time I didn't think that was studying!
[02:24.74]M: Yeah, it was fun! So you enjoyed it!
[02:28.42]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[02:34.01]1. How did the woman learn English?
[02:51.89]2. How did the woman deal with the words that she didn't understand?
[03:10.49]3. Why did the woman repeatedly watch The Blues Brothers?
[03:28.86]4. How does the woman feel about English learning?
[03:46.66]Conversation Two
[03:48.27]M: Alexandra, did you work at an airport before? 
[03:51.68]You said you worked in aviation.
[03:53.86]W: Yes, my previous job was writing contracts for an aviation company. 
[03:59.15]We bought and sold airplanes and aircraft engines, so we did a lot of marketing and leasing and communicating with people from different countries. 
[04:08.44]And sometimes airlines wanted to buy equipment, so we had a lot of negotiations.
[04:14.58]M: Can you explain what leasing is?
[04:17.06]W: Leasing is when our company owns a piece of equipment, either an airplane or an engine, and a customer has a need. 
[04:25.08]For example, if their airplane has to do some maintenance, and they need a replacement, then we will let them use our airplane for a certain number of months, like you rent a car.
[04:36.44]M: Oh, wow! And you lease not only the planes but engines?
[04:40.59]W: Sometimes you have an airplane that is delayed at the airport because of some reason and they need to swap an engine out or whatever.
[04:48.31]M: Right before the plane takes off, they sometimes switch the engine?
[04:52.25]W: They'll take the passengers off and put them on another plane because it takes a lot longer than the 10 or 15 minutes turnaround, but, you will have...it's more than an emergency type of situation, so they'll take the engine off, and it might be an overnight deal so we go ahead and furnish a replacement engine until they can move that plane back to where it belongs or have the engine repaired.
[05:17.16]M: So can you lease a pilot?
[05:19.35]W: Yes! You can lease a crew; it's called a wet lease. 
[05:23.86]And we used to do dry leases meaning we only provided the equipment but a wet lease includes a full crew that will fly the airplane, flight attendants, etc.
[05:35.19]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[05:41.52]5. What was the woman's previous job?
[06:00.86]6. What does the woman say about ¡°leasing¡±?
[06:20.03]7. Why do they put the passengers on another plane when switching an engine?
[06:41.56]8. What is included in a dry lease?
